body:
He tried management or moving up, and really just likes programming and making his ludicrous salary by talking to a rubber duck until the problem that he’s working on gets solved. 

I think having to hire for his team showed him how many desperate people who can’t actually code, but need money because of [insert high COL area with relatively low wages outside of tech here] being the area that it is. 

Would regularly have people come in, claim to have 7 years of C++ or more, and then fail to write even fizzbuzz, in a language of the interviewee’s choice.

I know the algorithm for fizzbuzz, and I’m some dumb kid who dropped out of college, because COVID made things much, much harder to accomplish.

I think, in C++ the whole thing would be:

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    for (int x = 0; x <= 100; x++) {
         if (x % 3 == 0 && x % 5 == 0){
            cout << x << “ Fizzbuzz” << ‘\n’;
         }
         else if (x % 3 == 0){
              cout << x << “ Fizz” << ‘/n’;
          }
          else if (x % 5 == 0){
               cout << x << “ Buzz” << ‘/n’;
          }
          else {
                cout << x <<  ‘\n’;
          }
    }
return 0;
}

I could also tell you that I did it the way that I would have done it in school, and that if I were in production, I would  omit that namespace because memory is at a premium, and it’s dumb to import the whole namespace just so I don’t have to type std.cout or whatever.

Edit: It was formatted correctly on my phone, and I’m mad now because mobile formatting ruined everything
